---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const user = Astro.locals.user;
const seo = {
  title: 'Business Submission Policy | CrossLinkd',
  description: 'What we accept, what we reject, and what gets a listing removed: the complete submission and quality policy for the CrossLinkd directory.',
  path: '/submission-policy',
};
---
<BaseLayout user={user} seo={seo}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold">Business submission policy</h1>
    <p class="section-sub">What we accept, what we reject, and what gets a listing removed. A rejection is a directory decision, not a verification of the listings that remain.</p>

    <div class="prose-custom mt-8 space-y-6 text-[15px] leading-relaxed" style="color:var(--text-soft)">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold" style="color:var(--text)">What we accept</h2>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
          <li>Businesses whose owners identify them as Christian-owned. That identification is owner-submitted. CrossLinkd does not independently confirm it.</li>
          <li>Churches, ministries, nonprofits, and Christian schools that provide a public name and a way to contact them.</li>
          <li>Individual professionals who list under their own name. Any credential they mention is their statement, not a CrossLinkd check.</li>
          <li>Online businesses that provide ownership contact details. Those details are not independently verified by default.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold" style="color:var(--text)">What we reject</h2>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
          <li>Duplicate listings for the same business (submit one; we will link additional locations).</li>
          <li>Incomplete submissions: no working phone, no service area or address, template filler text.</li>
          <li>Listings that are incomplete or that contradict themselves in an obvious way. CrossLinkd does not judge the sincerity of a faith claim.</li>
          <li>Anything illegal, or that violates our <a href="/guidelines" class="underline">community guidelines</a>.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold" style="color:var(--text)">Quality standards for published listings</h2>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
          <li>Name, category, hours, and contact details should be filled in. A completeness review does not confirm that they are still true.</li>
          <li>Descriptions describe the business, not a search-engine keyword list.</li>
          <li>Reviews follow the <a href="/reviews-policy" class="underline">review &amp; moderation policy</a>; owners may not review their own business.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 id="removal" class="text-xl font-extrabold" style="color:var(--text)">Correction and removal</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">To ask for a correction or removal, use the <a href="/contact?topic=report" class="underline">contact form</a>. A request is community reported. It is not proof that CrossLinkd has already investigated the business. Copyright reports use the <a href="/copyright" class="underline">copyright page</a>.</p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
          <li>A listing the owner no longer maintains may be marked Inactive.</li>
          <li>A license claim that the owner cannot explain may be removed from the text. CrossLinkd does not itself check license databases.</li>
          <li>Repeated inability to reach the contact channel the owner provided.</li>
          <li>Fraud, misrepresentation, or patterns in reviews that suggest deception.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2">Owners are always told why, and can respond through the <a href="/appeals" class="underline">appeals process</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold" style="color:var(--text)">Timing</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">A listing may publish as owner-submitted before anyone reviews it for completeness. If we decline or ask for a fix, we should say why. Do not read silence as a verification.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>
